    # For ".hidden.txt", final dot at position before txt, so ".txt"
    # So Go-like Ext: find last dot in basename, if dot exists, return substring from dot, else "".
    # That will give ".hidden" for ".hidden".
    # For Python, we can implement similarly.

    # We'll recompute ext Go-like:
    base = filename
    idx = base.rfind('.')
    if idx != -1:
